{
  "source": "course-assets/layers/layers.mp4",
  "duration": 176.0,
  "segments": [
    {
      "start": 0.0,
      "end": 4.78,
      "text": "Have you ever read a passage in English class that only made sense after a few reads?"
    },
    {
      "start": 5.34,
      "end": 6.14,
      "text": "Try this sentence."
    },
    {
      "start": 7.1,
      "end": 9.22,
      "text": "The horse raced past the barn fell."
    },
    {
      "start": 10.02,
      "end": 11.94,
      "text": "On the first read, it doesn't make sense."
    },
    {
      "start": 12.4,
      "end": 13.94,
      "text": "It feels like someone forgot a word."
    },
    {
      "start": 14.42,
      "end": 17.38,
      "text": "You reach fell and the sentence just seems to stop short."
    },
    {
      "start": 17.92,
      "end": 19.0,
      "text": "So you read it again."
    },
    {
      "start": 19.6,
      "end": 20.98,
      "text": "Wait, did a barn fall?"
    },
    {
      "start": 21.22,
      "end": 23.52,
      "text": "Or did the horse raced past the barn afterward?"
    },
    {
      "start": 24.1,
      "end": 28.98,
      "text": "You test each possibility against the words to see if fell goes with the barn or with the horse."
    },
    {
      "start": 28.98,
      "end": 30.9,
      "text": "Finally, the meaning clicks."
    },
    {
      "start": 31.54,
      "end": 34.62,
      "text": "Someone raced a horse past a barn, then the horse fell."
    },
    {
      "start": 35.22,
      "end": 38.2,
      "text": "Raced describes a horse, and fell is what the horse did."
    },
    {
      "start": 38.74,
      "end": 41.98,
      "text": "Working the sentence out depends entirely on these repeated passes."
    },
    {
      "start": 42.58,
      "end": 44.78,
      "text": "Each read updates the meaning until it clicks."
    },
    {
      "start": 45.82,
      "end": 47.02,
      "text": "AI does something similar."
    },
    {
      "start": 47.44,
      "end": 49.58,
      "text": "It builds meaning through repeated updates."
    },
    {
      "start": 50.02,
      "end": 52.08,
      "text": "AI doesn't read your message the way you do."
    },
    {
      "start": 52.3,
      "end": 54.76,
      "text": "It processes your text through a series of layers."
    },
    {
      "start": 55.22,
      "end": 58.14,
      "text": "The whole stack of layers is called a neural network."
    },
    {
      "start": 58.14,
      "end": 62.16,
      "text": "numbers go in on one side, and final numbers come out the other."
    },
    {
      "start": 62.74,
      "end": 66.46,
      "text": "In between stands a long line of layers, one after another,"
    },
    {
      "start": 66.9,
      "end": 69.22,
      "text": "each containing attention and transformation."
    },
    {
      "start": 69.98,
      "end": 74.54,
      "text": "The numbers that come out are not the numbers that went in. Attention and transformation"
    },
    {
      "start": 74.54,
      "end": 78.44,
      "text": "update the numbers at each layer. Now, let's follow a single"
    },
    {
      "start": 78.44,
      "end": 82.24,
      "text": "word, it, to see how its numbers change in a real sentence."
    },
    {
      "start": 82.84,
      "end": 85.72,
      "text": "The tired cat sat on the mat during the May rainstorm."
    },
    {
      "start": 85.72,
      "end": 87.2,
      "text": "It soon fell asleep."
    },
    {
      "start": 87.9,
      "end": 90.78,
      "text": "At the start, the word it could refer to different things."
    },
    {
      "start": 91.36,
      "end": 96.28,
      "text": "The starting numbers .12 and negative .34 don't tell us which one."
    },
    {
      "start": 96.86,
      "end": 102.06,
      "text": "By layer 1, the numbers update, beginning to capture a connection between it and cat."
    },
    {
      "start": 102.72,
      "end": 105.36,
      "text": "Moving into layer 2, the numbers update again."
    },
    {
      "start": 105.88,
      "end": 109.34,
      "text": "Now they carry even more specific information about that connection."
    },
    {
      "start": 110.06,
      "end": 111.12,
      "text": "This process repeats."
    },
    {
      "start": 111.52,
      "end": 113.1,
      "text": "It doesn't stop at layer 2."
    },
    {
      "start": 113.1,
      "end": 119.1,
      "text": "the numbers continue passing through more layers, each building directly on the previous layer's numbers."
    },
    {
      "start": 119.8,
      "end": 124.34,
      "text": "By the result stage, the two numbers finish at 0.41 and 0.06."
    },
    {
      "start": 125.16,
      "end": 128.98,
      "text": "Its updated numbers carry information about its connection to CAT."
    },
    {
      "start": 129.72,
      "end": 133.96,
      "text": "While AI companies don't always share exactly how many layers their models use,"
    },
    {
      "start": 134.42,
      "end": 139.14,
      "text": "published designs show architectures built with dozens and sometimes more than a hundred layers."
    },
    {
      "start": 139.14,
      "end": 142.42,
      "text": "The horse sentence took a few reeds to untangle."
    },
    {
      "start": 143.16,
      "end": 147.72,
      "text": "Sarcasm, story twists, and complicated reasoning can take even more work."
    },
    {
      "start": 148.32,
      "end": 152.5,
      "text": "AI's layers give it more steps to work through those relationships and build meaning."
    },
    {
      "start": 153.04,
      "end": 157.56,
      "text": "If more layers give the system better reasoning, why not just keep adding them infinitely?"
    },
    {
      "start": 158.18,
      "end": 163.04,
      "text": "Because adding layers demands massive amounts of computing power and time, the extra"
    },
    {
      "start": 163.04,
      "end": 164.78,
      "text": "benefit has to be worth the cost."
    },
    {
      "start": 164.78,
      "end": 171.72,
      "text": "Meaning builds up, layer by layer, attention and transformation, dozens of times."
    }
  ],
